                <pb facs="0900" n="866" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v16/pg866"/>

                <head>409. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The Commander in Chief, Pacific, Admiral Herbert
                        Riley, and his Assistant Political Adviser, Thomas Corcoran, visited Vientiane September
                    24–26. They held discussions with the members of the Country Team and with all
                    the political officers in the Embassy. Riley’s account of the visit is in CINCPAC telegram 5849 to the Joint Chiefs of Staff, September 29.
                    (Department of State, EA Files: Lot 68 D 77, Laos 1960, Part I) Corcoran wrote his own impressions of the trip
                    in a memorandum to Sterling Cottrell, CINCPAC
                    POLAD, September 30. (Washington National
                    Records Center, OSD/ISA Files: FRC 64 A 2170, 092 Asia) Cottrell sent a letter to
                        Parsons on October 1 explaining his
                    view of the visit and providing Parsons a
                    copy of Corcoran’s memorandum.
                    (Department of State, FE/SEA (Laos) Files: Lot
                    65 D 169, 350 Pol Affairs, 10/60 Laos)</p>
                <p>All these documents are included in <ref target="frus:frus1958-60v15-16mSupp1"
                        >the microfiche supplement</ref>.</p>
            </div>
